{
  "requirement": "`OutlineContent::language()` returns the name of the `OutlineLang` that produced\nthe snapshot. The root and each selected item report the same name. An explicit\nprovider supplies its own name, including when the filename would select a\ndifferent language by default.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.outlines.language`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. The root's `language()` returns the name of the `OutlineLang` that produced the snapshot.\n2. Each selected item reports the same name as the root.\n3. An explicit provider supplies its own name, even when the filename would select a different language by default.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[default_language_names_match_the_retained_outline]` builds roots through the default path. It covers the filenames `LIB.RS`, `widget.TSX`, `README` and `foo.unknown`. It asserts that `root.language()` equals `rust`, `tsx`, `plain-text` and `plain-text`, and equals `languages::name_for_path`. This covers the default language choice, including case-insensitive extensions and the fallback to plain text.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[explicit_languages_share_configuration_and_retain_their_scheme]` uses a `CustomLanguage` named `custom` with the misleading filename `misleading.rs`. It checks this through both `from_source_with` and `from_path_with`, and asserts `root.language() == \"custom\"` for each. This covers the \"explicit provider supplies its own name, even when the filename would select a different language\" clause. The same test asserts `selected.language() == \"custom\"` after `select(\"part[selected]\")`, which covers the selected-item clause.\n\n**Gap check**\n- Selected items under a default language are not tested. This is not a gap. In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#impl[OutlineContent]/fn[language]`, `language()` returns `&self.snapshot.language`. That is a pass-through of the shared snapshot, so the selected-item test with the explicit provider exercises the same path. Nothing in the text distinguishes selection by language kind.\n- I found no other relevant tests, and there are no acknowledgments.",
